WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.488
Open Disaster Recovery from Operations.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.100
Add or review the datacenter, its Foundation endpoint and dependency

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:07.762
reviews.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.325
Link a complete Foundation V M configuration and the cluster post-configuration

00:00:13.338 --> 00:00:15.475
pipeline to a recovery profile.

00:00:15.888 --> 00:00:19.400
Use existing cluster to rebuild for re-foundation.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.162
Recovery reconstructs infrastructure.

00:00:22.538 --> 00:00:26.475
Restoring virtual machines and applications remains the responsibility

00:00:26.488 --> 00:00:28.425
of your backup and recovery platform.

00:00:29.588 --> 00:00:34.250
Review Profile shows the captured deployment and pipeline snapshots Check

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:39.182
the exact cluster name address physical node serials images

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.725
networks and every configuration step The status is calculated from the

00:00:43.725 --> 00:00:48.608
latest revision and its source files Baseline changed means a source file

00:00:48.725 --> 00:00:53.162
pipeline or datacenter Foundation endpoint no longer matches the reviewed

00:00:53.162 --> 00:00:58.108
snapshot To adopt the intended current settings choose Capture New Revision

00:00:58.388 --> 00:01:03.275
save the draft inspect its targets enter Baseline review notes and select

00:01:03.275 --> 00:01:08.025
Mark Baseline Reviewed Marking the old snapshot reviewed does not clear a

00:01:08.025 --> 00:01:13.382
continuing mismatch Capture New Revision is the current profile editing path

00:01:13.538 --> 00:01:18.300
and retains earlier revisions The current interface has no profile delete

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:23.382
action Baseline review does not image hardware Prepare a run

00:01:23.388 --> 00:01:28.595
only after review then obtain the separate exact-content deployment approval

00:01:28.712 --> 00:01:33.658
and destructive confirmations Deployed rehearsals also make real changes

00:01:34.046 --> 00:01:38.758
Enter the required cluster and Foundation confirmation phrases, acknowledge

00:01:38.758 --> 00:01:41.046
the imaging scope, and deploy once.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.008
Follow the linked job and Foundation session.

00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:48.796
A non-JSON response or H T T P four twenty-nine can be

00:01:48.796 --> 00:01:52.208
a transport or rate-limit issue while imaging continues.

00:01:52.608 --> 00:01:56.620
Inspect the existing job and target state before retrying.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:00.670
Stop Orchestration does not prove that Foundation has stopped.

00:02:01.879 --> 00:02:06.166
After confirmed deployment success, use the initial access bootstrap

00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:10.216
when the captured pipeline begins with eligible password and EULA

00:02:10.454 --> 00:02:11.441
or Pulse settings.

00:02:11.829 --> 00:02:16.316
Obtain each required exact-content approval and acknowledge the cluster.

00:02:16.729 --> 00:02:19.516
Run only the permitted narrow bootstrap prefix.

00:02:19.929 --> 00:02:23.179
This removes the need to log in manually just to change the

00:02:23.179 --> 00:02:25.541
initial password before health collection.

00:02:25.954 --> 00:02:29.666
Broader cluster configuration still waits for verification.

00:02:30.837 --> 00:02:35.600
Collect P E Health Readbacks using the reviewed post-bootstrap credential

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.712
and verified certificate trust.

00:02:38.125 --> 00:02:42.700
Check cluster identity, complete expected membership and explicitly

00:02:42.712 --> 00:02:43.537
reported health.

00:02:43.925 --> 00:02:48.912
Missing fields, authentication failures or network errors remain unknown.

00:02:49.325 --> 00:02:54.887
If automatic evidence is unavailable, independently verify P E and

00:02:54.887 --> 00:02:57.862
record the manual attestation with its evidence reference.

00:02:58.262 --> 00:03:02.837
Begin remaining configuration within fifteen minutes of fresh evidence.

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:07.479
Run the remaining eligible steps from the captured snapshots.

00:03:07.866 --> 00:03:13.066
If a step fails, reconcile actual state and continue only the unfinished

00:03:13.066 --> 00:03:13.454
work.

00:03:13.841 --> 00:03:18.029
Where approval policy requires a direct job, run the exact approved

00:03:18.029 --> 00:03:21.854
snapshot and link its successful job to the pending step.

00:03:22.266 --> 00:03:25.679
Do not repeat successful imaging or password changes.

00:03:26.129 --> 00:03:29.854
Finish with independent acceptance and an explicit handoff to the

00:03:29.866 --> 00:03:32.454
backup platform for workload restoration.
